# Unicode CLDR, cldr-json cldr-dates-full/main/ha/dateFields.json.
# relative-type-1: "sati na gaba" / "wata na gaba", the week or month ahead.
# The marker trails its noun.
#
# CLDR's weekday form "Laraba mai zuwa" (the coming Wednesday) is the other
# half of the field and is deliberately NOT shipped: it ends in zuwa, which is
# also this locale's range terminator ("daga Litinin zuwa Jumaʼa"), and the
# range split reads the raw token stream before multiword surfaces are glued
# back together.  Shipping it would let "Litinin mai zuwa" be read as the open
# range "up to Monday" -- a wrong answer rather than no answer -- so the
# surface stays out until the two can be told apart.
na gaba
mai zuwa
